  "notes": [
    "Pencil page1, no date. The page sets up a complete noetherian discretely valued ring V, residue field k and fraction field K, then states the cyclic/Kummer description when the indicated characteristic is zero and k is algebraically closed. It identifies K*/K*n by valuation and writes the absolute Galois group as T_infty(k). The lower case removes completeness and introduces a prime-to-p quotient. The overwritten characteristic sign and several short forms remain explicit doubts.",
    "The source spells cyclique and kummerienne in the singular after Les extens. Those endings are not regularized. The compressed heading is read Gpe galoisien; H supplies a separate cancelled Théor and a subsequent Théorie that the crop does not distinguish as two words. The final k is identified from the same mu_n(k) notation above; the overwritten argument of car is kept k/K because the two writing layers cannot be ordered. The Z in the parenthetical profinite completion is shaped like 2, as are the two quotient Z letters; the local recurring notation identifies it as Z, not the numeral2. No general classification theorem is proved in this transcription run."
  ],
  "hand": [
    "On scan002 the k has a long stem and compact looped arms and can look like K or R after retracing; the two unambiguous mu_n(k) positions control the final occurrence, but not the overwrite order in car. Z is often rounded like2; the repeated Z/nZ examples establish that local shape. Short French words are extremely compressed: C and H expand corps-residue/fraction labels and H expands prem to premier; uncertain residue letters are retained."
  ],
